# HAOS Apps repository

This is a multi-app Home Assistant repository at `github.com/byte-bridge/haos-apps`.

Target **Home Assistant OS** only. See [docs/HOME_ASSISTANT_ADRS.md](docs/HOME_ASSISTANT_ADRS.md). Supervised was dropped in [discussion #1198](https://github.com/home-assistant/architecture/discussions/1198); [ADR-0013 Container](https://github.com/home-assistant/architecture/blob/master/adr/0013-home-assistant-container.md) has no Supervisor/apps.

## Structure

- App folders live at the **repo root** (e.g. `rancher/`), each with a `config.yaml`
- `repository.yaml` registers the repo with Home Assistant
- `templates/app/` is the scaffold for new apps — copy it, don't modify in place (`config.yaml.example` → `config.yaml`)
- Shared docs go in `docs/`

## When adding or editing an app

1. Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/ADDING_AN_APP.md`
2. Follow [HA app configuration](https://developers.home-assistant.io/docs/apps/configuration)
3. Use [home-assistant/apps-example](https://github.com/home-assistant/apps-example) for packaging/layout/CI — not for Rancher’s privileged Docker wrapper
4. Use `#!/usr/bin/with-contenv bashio` for shell scripts with LF line endings
5. Update the apps table in root `README.md`
6. Document security requirements (Protection mode, privileged access) in `DOCS.md`

## Code style

- Minimal, focused diffs — one app per change when possible
- Match existing patterns in sibling apps (see `rancher/` for Docker wrapper pattern)
- Don't pin Alpine package versions unless required
- Don't commit secrets or create git commits unless asked
